  "reason": "Evidence: The current best result is config_049 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.629 acc, a large jump over singleprofile (~0.535). In singleprofile, concat and weighted fusion were nearly identical (0.535 vs 0.532), but we have no evidence about fusion in the multiprofile+aggregation regime where the dynamics may differ. Question: config_050 changes only the fusion method (weighted vs concat) while holding all other settings identical to config_049, cleanly isolating the fusion effect in the multiprofile+avgpool context. Why best next: It is a minimal one-variable A/B comparison against the current best, directly reducing uncertainty about whether weighted fusion interacts beneficially with multiprofile aggregation. The answer will determine whether to keep concat or switch to weighted for all subsequent multiprofile experiments, making it the highest-information-per-budget choice before exploring RNA encoders or image backbones."
}

